<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::logistics_resilience" target="us_china_tech_trade::ai_compute_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Degraded logistics resilience (port closures, damaged transit routes, insurance and transit delays) directly delays or cancels shipments of GPUs/accelerators and rack systems from East Asian manufacturers to cloud providers and data centers in China, reducing deployed AI compute capacity there and in aggregated cross-border deployments.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::logistics_resilience" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::oil_supply_shortfall" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved logistics resilience (clearing, storage, and alternative routing) in the Russia–Ukraine theater preserves export flows and emergency stock rotations, directly reducing the risk of a measurable physical oil supply shortfall in global markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
