<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_pressure" target="north_korea_nuclear::geopolitical_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising reciprocal escalation in the Russia–Ukraine theater raises great-power threat perceptions and produces more assertive military and diplomatic postures by Russia, China and the United States in other theaters, increasing strategic rivalry around the Korean Peninsula.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">north_korea_nuclear</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_pressure" target="us_china_tech_trade::crossborder_restriction" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in escalation (high-profile uses of force and reciprocal provocations) rapidly elevates US/EU threat perceptions and domestic political pressure, producing fast-moving executive actions and regulatory expansions (export controls, investment screening, sanctions) that increase trade and tech-transfer barriers vis-à-vis China.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_trade</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_pressure" target="us_debt_bond_stress::market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising escalation pressure (reciprocal strikes, provocative acts) directly raises short-term risk premia and urgency in hedging demand, producing immediate spikes in realized and implied volatility across bond and related markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_debt_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_pressure" target="us_iran_gulf_conflict::regional_escalation_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising escalation pressure in the Russia–Ukraine war drives Washington and NATO to reallocate naval and air deterrent assets to Europe and signals heightened great-power competition, which reduces perceived US capacity/deterrence in the Gulf and encourages Iranian forces and proxies to probe or escalate, raising regional escalation risk.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
