  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp increases in crude/oil prices raise electricity and cooling costs for data centers and shipping/installation costs for hardware, reducing the economic incentive to commission new large‑scale AI compute deployments and delaying capacity expansions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_iran_gulf_conflict</data>
