  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A rapid rise in DPRK nuclear-related strategic tensions increases market risk premia and short-term hedging demand, lifting benchmark crude prices even without direct supply disruptions in the Gulf.</data>
